WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:03.048
- So, a couple of your older
projects have gotten new life.

00:00:03.048 --> 00:00:03.930
I don't know if you know this,

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.450
but we hear that there's a
potential "Freaky Friday" sequel

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:08.730
and "Summer School" is blowing up online.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.500
Like, did you expect that 35 years later?

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.910
That is, it's all blowing up.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:12.990
Like, people are wanting the sequel

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.790
and now they're talking about this again.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:19.080
- Well, the first one is because
Jamie's talking about it.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.220
- Yeah.
- And you know Jamie.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.053
- [Kelly] Yeah. I love Jamie.

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:21.886
- Right? I do too.
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:21.886 --> 00:00:23.640
- And I've known her since she was 15, so.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.473
- [Kelly] Oh, wow.

00:00:24.473 --> 00:00:26.520
- If she's talking about
it, then it'll happen.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:27.540
- [Kelly] It's probably gonna happen.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.770
- 'Cause all things happen.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:29.967
- Yes.
- That's right.

00:00:29.967 --> 00:00:31.980
- But it's, did you ever
expect the other one though?

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.279
Summer, what? Like for 35 years later?

00:00:33.279 --> 00:00:34.945
- "Summer School"?
- Yeah. "Summer School."

00:00:34.945 --> 00:00:36.480
Sorry.
- Yeah, no, no. Yeah, no.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.674
- I was just so thrilled that Carl Reiner

00:00:38.674 --> 00:00:40.740
was interested in me to play this part.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.320
And then my wife read the
script at the same time.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.360
Said, "don't go near this. Don't do this."

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.067
But we have very different
opinions of material and-

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:48.450
- Yeah.
- Things like that,

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.797
which is healthy, but I just said,

00:00:50.797 --> 00:00:52.230
"He thinks I can do this."

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.850
- Yeah.
- So, I'm gonna do it.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.137
- Yeah.
- So, I went and did it.

00:00:55.137 --> 00:00:55.970
- I love that.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.697
- And all those kids, you know?

00:00:57.697 --> 00:00:58.530
(audience applauding)

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.420
- But I love that it's
like blowing back up.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.800
I just think it's cool
when it comes back around.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.210
It's like music, people like Mike,

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.043
I hear young kids-

00:01:04.043 --> 00:01:04.876
- Yeah, great soundtrack.
- Talking about music

00:01:04.876 --> 00:01:06.030
and I'm like, that's like from the '70s.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:06.863
Like, what?
- Yeah.

00:01:06.863 --> 00:01:07.696
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:07.696 --> 00:01:09.930
And all those people were young

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.443
and just starting out at that time, right?

00:01:11.443 --> 00:01:12.600
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.820
- So, those kids were all over 30

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.530
when they were playing
high school kids, so.

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:17.363
- Of course.

00:01:17.363 --> 00:01:19.567
- Every one of 'em had an
idea after every scene.

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:21.810
"Hey, Carl, hey Carl,
hey Carl. Can I do this?"

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.580
And he'd go, "Ha ha ha ha. No."

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:24.576
- No. (chuckles)
(audience laughs)

00:01:24.576 --> 00:01:25.409
Stick to it.

00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:27.777
- Yeah, and but so many
of the little threads

00:01:27.777 --> 00:01:29.250
at the end of every scene

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.460
that he let the camera
roll on are in that film.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:33.293
- Oh, cool.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:35.280
- And I had a chance to
work with him later years

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.790
laying down a track for
the movie years later.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:39.623
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:39.623 --> 00:01:42.480
- And a chance to sit with him
for four hours and do that.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.460
And I loved that opportunity

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.200
to finally tell him what he meant to me.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.163
- Oh, that's so cool.

00:01:47.163 --> 00:01:48.390
- [Mark] Yep.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:49.770
- Yeah, you like to tell people that.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.480
I like that about you so
far in this interview.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.740
You like to like, let people know

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.570
that they like made a change
and an impact in your life.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:55.403
That's cool.

00:01:55.403 --> 00:01:56.400
- I was telling you that on the way out.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.130
- Well, nobody, not
everybody does that. Yeah.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:01:59.963
- Why?

00:01:59.963 --> 00:02:01.080
- I don't know.
(audience laughs)

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.700
I don't know. Maybe they
feel foolish or whatever?

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.720
But like yeah.
- You do that all the time.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.432
- I do, I'm like, well, I'm a
very chatty person in general,

00:02:06.432 --> 00:02:08.349
so I tell everybody everything.

00:02:08.349 --> 00:02:10.710
- There's a kindness in that.
- Yeah.

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:12.210
- It's not just being a chatty person.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.043
- Yeah.

00:02:13.043 --> 00:02:14.040
It makes me feel good to tell someone

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.623
that they've made a
big impact on me, yeah.

